<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">disenchant</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">disenchant</ansi> command removes a Chrysalis enchantment from an
item, severing the bond between the mutation and your gear.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Requirements ━━━</ansi>

  Station:   An <ansi fg="yellow">enchanting_circle</ansi> must be in the room with you.
  Item:      The enchanted item must be in your inventory, not equipped.
             Once disenchanted, the item returns to its original state.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Usage ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">disenchant <item></ansi>    Remove the enchantment from the named item.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Warning ━━━</ansi>

The separation between a mutation and its host item is not clean. When you sever
the bond, expect to feel temporarily weakened. The feeling will pass, but it may
take time.

